ngchiuli/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mingchiuli/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mingchiuli/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mingchiuli/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mingchiuli/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mingchiuli","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mingchiuli/megalith-micro/commits/6eaea91e06a20c5f14da9a33fe391703b9cffe5a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:59:56Z","email":"mingchiuli@163.com","name":"mingchiuli"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T02:21:32Z","email":"mingchiuli@163.com","name":"mingchiuli"},"message":"refactor: own paging in the application layer\n\nPaged use cases returned the shared PageAdapter envelope from common-contract,\nwhich is also the HTTP and RPC payload shape, so the core was bound to the wire\nformat. Each application now owns an application.model.Page carrying the same\nbounds, and the page''s own type flows through ports and services:\n\n- the readers, repositories, and the blog query adapter build the core page\n- services derive their page with withContent(...) instead of a builder\n- the new adapter.in.http.PageResponse renders the core page as the PageAdapter\n  clients receive, and micro-search''s SearchPage is renamed to Page so the four\n  applications use one name for the same concept\n- common-arch bans common.page from domain and application, so the envelope\n  cannot return to the core","tree":{"sha":"bb12dd27d469a2bf361428f1ce823f0f06713481","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mingchiuli/megalith-micro/git/trees/bb12dd27d469a2bf361428f1ce823f0f06713481"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mingchiuli/megalith-micro/git/commits/6eaea91e06a20c5f14da9a33fe391703b9cffe5a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committ