ingchiuli","id":80095372,"login":"mingchiuli","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMDk1Mzcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mingchiuli/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mingchiuli/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mingchiuli/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mingchiuli/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mingchiuli/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mingchiuli","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mingchiuli/megalith-micro/commits/1f03b3c4667ad829a494257836ffa6da642befc6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T12:38:14Z","email":"mingchiuli@163.com","name":"mingchiuli"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T12:38:14Z","email":"mingchiuli@163.com","name":"mingchiuli"},"message":"refactor(user): align the service with the README layout\n\nThe eight JPA entities sink into adapter.out.persistence.entity behind framework-free domain records and a persistence mapper. Because the repositories implemented the read ports themselves, each one now keeps only its Spring Data queries and a JPA reader adapter maps to the domain. The seventeen config/convertor mappers dissolve into application models and adapter mappers, the password encoder and password-lock settings move behind ports and wiring, and the thirteen services are declared as beans in config.","tree":{"sha":"08e8da961192ca641e0335d629e622a58264b535","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mingchiuli/megalith-micro/git/trees/08e8da961192ca641e0335d629e622a58264b535"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mingchiuli/megalith-micro/git/commits/1f03b3c4667ad829a494257836ffa6da642befc6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80095372?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mingch