url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commits/6976ae89a275f73e492aa197af5cfdef5b44f942/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T17:11:29Z","email":"estebanburgos85@gmail.com","name":"Esteban Burgos"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T17:11:29Z","email":"estebanburgos85@gmail.com","name":"Esteban Burgos"},"message":"feat(ui): sidebar edge toggle with built-in persistence and adaptive content padding — Spec 07 rev 1.1\n\nReview feedback on the original pin implementation:\n\n- the toggle moves from a padlock in the header to a subtle circular arrow\n  button on the sidebar''s outer edge (ChevronRight collapsed / ChevronLeft\n  pinned), visible in both states; keeps aria-pressed and\n  data-tucu=\"sidebar-pin\", titles now ''Expand menu''/''Collapse menu''\n- fix: toggle flips the PINNED state, not the visual open state, and the\n  aside''s hover-expansion ignores pointers entering through the toggle —\n  otherwise the expanding sidebar moved the button away mid-click and it\n  could never be pinned with a real mouse\n- AdminLayout derives the effective pinned state and pads its content to the\n  expanded width (288px xl / 320px 2xl) while pinned, so the sidebar never\n  covers content, with transition-[padding]\n- pinned state now persists in the library: uncontrolled mode reads/writes\n  useTheme().isSidebarPinned (theme-storage localStorage key), undefined\n  until first toggle so defaultPinned governs the first visit; controlled\n  mode still bypasses the store for custom storages\n- docs: SidebarPinningSection updated to the edge-toggle semantics and the\n  built-in persistence; demo now shows an unmistakable per-state brand swap\n  (''Acme Admin'' wordmark expanded vs amber compact mark collapsed)\n- MCP resources synced (layouts, theme, styling-overrides); spec 07 amended\n  with revision 1.1 notes\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b07aa1e49807d4e8b1e69e255537ce8b65dc1238","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/git/trees/b07aa1e49807d4e8b1e69e255537ce8b65dc1238"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/git/commits/6976ae89a275f73e492aa197af5cfdef5b44f942","verification":{"payload":"tree b07aa1e49807d4e8b1e69e255537ce8b65dc1238\nparent 67efc370c16a9ccf8a757e63fc27232ac9f3778d\nauthor Esteban Burgos <estebanburgos85@gmail.com> 1787073089 -0300\ncommitter Esteban Burgos <estebanburgos85@gmail.com> 1787073089 -0300\n\nfeat(ui): sidebar edge toggle with built-in persistence and adaptive content padding — Spec 07 rev 1.1\n\nReview feedback on the original pin implementation:\n\n- the toggle moves from a padlock in the header to a subtle circular arrow\n  button on the sidebar''s outer edge (ChevronRight collapsed / ChevronLeft\n  pinned), visible in both states; keeps aria-pressed and\n  data-tucu=\"sidebar-pin\", titles now ''Expand menu''/''Collapse menu''\n- fix: toggle flips the PINNED state, not the visual open state, and the\n  aside''s hover-expansion ignores pointers entering through the toggle —\n  otherwise the expanding sidebar moved the button away mid-click and it\n  could never be pinned with a real mouse\n- AdminLayout derives the effective pinned state and pads its content to the\n  expanded width (288px xl / 320px 2xl) while pinned, so the sidebar never\n  covers content, with transition-[padding]\n- pinned state now persists in the library: uncontrolled mode reads/writes\n  useTheme().isSidebarPinned (theme-storage localStorage key), undefined\n  until first toggle so defaultPinned governs the first visit; controlled\n  mode still bypasses the store for custom storages\n- docs: SidebarPinningSection updated to the edge-toggle semantics and the\n  built-in persistence; demo now shows an unmistakable per-state brand swap\n  (''Acme Admin'' wordmark expanded vs amber compact mark collapsed)\n- MCP resources synced (layouts, theme, styling-overrides); spec 07 amended\n  with revision 1.1 notes\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgW0Xzwxyw7EbDV9DSOn/ap7+0ee\nwK0skFba86dVZgcpQAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJfx/xecIRhSMHsTjRVSRL8LU2IY3Ya0n3jUIeRrJU+r80JB9HEQFQ2m3qTgJtZDv5\nz4hfw2jdfkkqSJrxvniQE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T17:11:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71472902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos","id":71472902,"login":"e-burgos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDcyOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commit/6976ae89a275f73e492aa197af5cfdef5b44f942","node_id":"C_kwDOMrriatoAKDY5NzZhZTg5YTI3NWY3M2U0OTJhYTE5N2FmNWNmZGVmNWI0NGY5NDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commit/67efc370c16a9ccf8a757e63fc27232ac9f3778d","sha":"67efc370c16a9ccf8a757e63fc27232ac9f3778d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commits/67efc370c16a9ccf8a757e63fc27232ac9f3778d"}],"sha":"6976ae89a275f73e492aa