date":"2026-08-01T17:49:33Z","email":"estebanburgos85@gmail.com","name":"Esteban Burgos"},"message":"fix(test-lib): opt into the bundled fonts explicitly\n\nThe library''s theme entry no longer carries fonts (they were only ever\nreaching this app through the now-removed JS-side CSS injection), so load\nInter and JetBrains Mono the way an npm consumer would with\n`@import ''@e-burgos/tucu-ui/fonts''` — from the source file directly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"be5e1c244bad36e0fd26fcd74655f99bebad0825","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/git/trees/be5e1c244bad36e0fd26fcd74655f99bebad0825"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/git/commits/b0af29dda09bda0a5a55356858b98404c3d30d50","verification":{"payload":"tree be5e1c244bad36e0fd26fcd74655f99bebad0825\nparent f113492816bde765ac4ca7ce696fe06fbbe38a82\nauthor Esteban Burgos <estebanburgos85@gmail.com> 1785606573 -0300\ncommitter Esteban Burgos <estebanburgos85@gmail.com> 1785606573 -0300\n\nfix(test-lib): opt into the bundled fonts explicitly\n\nThe library''s theme entry no longer carries fonts (they were only ever\nreaching this app through the now-removed JS-side CSS injection), so load\nInter and JetBrains Mono the way an npm consumer would with\n`@import ''@e-burgos/tucu-ui/fonts''` — from the source file directly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgW0Xzwxyw7EbDV9DSOn/ap7+0ee\nwK0skFba86dVZgcpQAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQA7eht+X3O622A7tBrtrl0/3ZV2rlTaF5wUwPpoVmQWJzfVtEeIcr2/KspSKSgsuDc\nRByhpXoifZxDS26djCUQY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-01T18:36:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71472902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos","id":71472902,"login":"e-burgos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDcyOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commit/b0af29dda09bda0a5a55356858b98404c3d30d50","node_id":"C_kwDOMrriatoAKGIwYWYyOWRkYTA5YmRhMGE1YTU1MzU2ODU4Yjk4NDA0YzNkMzBkNTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commit/f113492816bde765ac4ca7ce696fe06fbbe38a82","sha":"f113492816bde765ac4ca7ce696fe06fbbe38a82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commits/f113492816bde765ac4ca7ce696fe06fbbe38a82"}],"sha":"b0af29dda09bda0a5a55356858b98404c3d30d50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commits/b0af29dda09bda0a5a55356858b98404c3d30d50"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71472902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos","id":71472902,"login":"e-burgos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDcyOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commits/f113492816bde765ac4ca7ce696fe06fbbe38a82/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-01T17:48:56Z","email":"estebanburgos85@gmail.com","name":"Esteban Burgos"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T17:48:56Z","email":"estebanburgos85@gmail.com","name":"Esteban Burgos"},"message":"feat(ui)!: ship CSS only through explicit entry points\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: the library no longer injects any stylesheet from its\nJavaScript module graph. Consumers bundling from source must import a CSS\nentry themselves (`./styles`, or `./theme` + their own Tailwind). npm\nconsumers are unaffected: the built modules never carried CSS imports.\nFonts now ship as woff2 files instead of base64; anything hotlinking\ndist/index.css must serve the adjacent fonts/ directory.\n\nTwo JS entry points pulled the same compiled Tailwind aggregate —\nsrc/index.ts via styles.css and theme-wrapper.tsx via assets/css/index.css\n— so every @font-face, keyframe and utility appeared twice in\ndist/index.css, and every app bundling the library from source received a\nfull second Tailwind build (~1 MB dead CSS). On top of that, Vite''s lib\nmode force-inlines CSS assets: 980 KB of variable fonts became 2.5 MB of\nbase64, 73% of the artifact.\n\n- Remove all four JS-side CSS imports (index.ts, theme-wrapper, datatable,\n  carousel) and delete the aggregate files they pulled.\n- Move the component-support CSS (datatable tokens, carousel skin, prism,\n  scrollbars, range slider, decorative backgrounds) into the theme.css\n  chain, so BOTH entries ship it exactly once. `./theme` consumers were\n  silently losing all of it — DataTable had no --color-table-* tokens at\n  all on that path.\n- Build dist/index.css, dist/fonts.css and dist/fonts/ in a dedicated\n  non-lib Vite pass (vite.config.styles.ts, chained from the main build):\n  fonts stay files, url()s stay relative.\n- Add the opt-in `./fonts` export (Inter + JetBrains Mono variable);\n  `./theme` deliberately excludes fonts so Tailwind consumers choose.\n- Scan only shipped source in globals.css @source — __tests__, docs-kit\n  and the ~1500 lucide re-export files no longer leak utilities into the\n  published stylesheet.\n- Replace deprecated `@variant dark` with `@custom-variant dark`, dropping\n  the duplicate definition in datatable.css.\n- Verify theme.css, fonts.css and the woff2 files in the publish script''s\n  required artifacts.\n\nMeasured: dist/index.css 3460 KB -> 661 KB (79 KB gzip), zero data: URIs,\nevery duplicated block now single. test-lib total CSS 1697 KB -> 806 KB\nwith an identical 3413-class inventory (zero classes lost) and its tucu-ui\nCSS chunk down from 932 KB to 15 KB. Suite: 489/489, MCP 113/113, lint 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8c2efadb3ab3a3d21e874e09f47a5802da16c8a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/git/trees/8c2efadb3ab3a3d21e874e09f47a5802da16c8a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/git/commits/f113492816bde765ac4ca7ce696fe06fbbe38a82","verification":{"payload":"tree 8c2efadb3ab3a3d21e874e09f47a5802da16c8a0\nparent 33843c0791f55a594481cde47d2693a4a1d69f01\nauthor Esteban Burgos <estebanburgos85@gmail.com> 1785606536 -0300\ncommitter Esteban Burgos <estebanburgos85@gmail.com> 1785606536 -0300\n\nfeat(ui)!: ship CSS only through explicit entry points\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: the library no longer injects any stylesheet from its\nJavaScript module graph. Consumers bundling from source must import a CSS\nentry themselves (`./styles`, or `./theme` + their own Tailwind). npm\nconsumers are unaffected: the built modules never carried CSS imports.\nFonts now ship as woff2 files instead of base64; anything hotlinking\ndist/index.css must serve the adjacent fonts/ directory.\n\nTwo JS entry points pulled the same compiled Tailwind aggregate —\nsrc/index.ts via styles.css and theme-wrapper.tsx via assets/css/index.css\n— so every @font-face, keyframe and utility appeared twice in\ndist/index.css, and every app bundling the library from source received a\nfull second Tailwind build (~1 MB dead CSS). On top of that, Vite''s lib\nmode force-inlines CSS assets: 980 KB of variable fonts became 2.5 MB of\nbase64, 73% of the artifact.\n\n- Remove all four JS-side CSS imports (index.ts, theme-wrapper, datatable,\n  carousel) and delete the aggregate files they pulled.\n- Move the component-support CSS (datatable tokens, carousel skin, prism,\n  scrollbars, range slider, decorative backgrounds) into the theme.css\n  chain, so BOTH entries ship it exactly once. `./theme` consumers were\n  silently losing all of it — DataTable had no --color-table-* tokens at\n  all on that path.\n- Build dist/index.css, dist/fonts.css and dist/fonts/ in a dedicated\n  non-lib Vite pass (vite.config.styles.ts, chained from the main build):\n  fonts stay files, url()s stay relative.\n- Add the opt-in `./fonts` export (Inter + JetBrains Mono variable);\n  `./theme` deliberately excludes fonts so Tailwind consumers choose.\n- Scan only shipped source in globals.css @source — __tests__, docs-kit\n  and the ~1500 lucide re-export files no longer leak utilities into the\n  published stylesheet.\n- Replace deprecated `@variant dark` with `@custom-variant dark`, dropping\n  the duplicate definition in datatable.css.\n- Verify theme.css, fonts.css and the woff2 files in the publish script''s\n  required artifacts.\n\nMeasured: dist/index.css 3460 KB -> 661 KB (79 KB gzip), zero data: URIs,\nevery duplicated block now single. test-lib total CSS 1697 KB -> 806 KB\nwith an identical 3413-class inventory (zero classes lost) and its tucu-ui\nCSS chunk down from 932 KB to 15 KB. Suite: 489/489, MCP 113/113, lint 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgW0Xzwxyw7EbDV9DSOn/ap7+0ee\nwK0skFba86dVZgcpQAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCy+a8c17X5vb5cdF7CH8/oX3HlOO4uED+OgSSm1wWf1H/Edpzpe+Xd3MtlBH1wzPv\nBuK1ZZYiZUWT944mRbtQA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-01T18:36:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71472902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos","id":71472902,"login":"e-burgos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDcyOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commit/f113492816bde765ac4ca7ce696fe06fbbe38a82","node_id":"C_kwDOMrriatoAKGYxMTM0OTI4MTZiZGU3NjVhYzRjYTdjZTY5NmZlMDZmYmJlMzhhODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commit/33843c0791f55a594481cde47d2693a4a1d69f01","sha":"33843c0791f55a594481cde47d2693a4a1d69f01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commits/33843c0791f55a594481cde47d2693a4a1d69f01"}],"sha":"f113492816bde765ac4ca7ce696fe06fbbe38a82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commits/f113492816bde765ac4ca7ce696fe06fbbe38a82"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71472902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos","id":71472902,"login":"e-burgos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDcyOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commits/33843c0791f55a594481cde47d2693a4a1d69f01/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-01T17:15:26Z","email":"estebanburgos85@gmail.com","name":"Esteban Burgos"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T17:15:26Z","email":"estebanburgos85@gmail.com","name":"Esteban Burgos"},"message":"fix(test-lib): scan the real sources and stop bundling Tailwind twice\n\ntest-lib got its stylesheet from two places and neither covered the docs\npages: the prebuilt dist/ui/tucu-ui/index.css, compiled by scanning only\nui/tucu-ui, and a bare `@import ''tailwindcss''`, whose automatic source\ndetection never leaves the Vite root. Anything used exclusively in\nui/tucu-docs was therefore never emitted — every `via-*` stop among them,\nso the feature-card gradients on the home page lost their middle colour or\nrendered grey.\n\nPoint the app at the library''s `./theme` entry instead of the compiled\n`./styles` one, as tucu-ui''s own docs prescribe for a consumer that runs\nits own Tailwind, and declare both source roots explicitly. Reading from\nui/tucu-ui/src rather than dist/ also means local library changes show up\nwithout rebuilding the package first, which is the reason this app exists.\n\nMeasured on a clean build: 4425 KB of CSS down to 1697 KB (-61.7%) while\nthe emitted class count rises from 3207 to 3413. The four classes that\ndisappear (bg-gray-700/90, border-gray-200, dark:bg-dark,\ndark:border-gray-700) are unused anywhere in the workspace.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fe9ded3b096dcfa36c4b73e9b98531f62995a5ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/git/trees/fe9ded3b096dcfa36c4b73e9b98531f62995a5ff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/git/commits/33843c0791f55a594481cde47d2693a4a1d69f01","verification":{"payload":"tree fe9ded3b096dcfa36c4b73e9b98531f62995a5ff\nparent 04710e7a42c871aacdfa71095ff43c7657527f63\nauthor Esteban Burgos <estebanburgos85@gmail.com> 1785604526 -0300\ncommitter Esteban Burgos <estebanburgos85@gmail.com> 1785604526 -0300\n\nfix(test-lib): scan the real sources and stop bundling Tailwind twice\n\ntest-lib got its stylesheet from two places and neither covered the docs\npages: the prebuilt dist/ui/tucu-ui/index.css, compiled by scanning only\nui/tucu-ui, and a bare `@import ''tailwindcss''`, whose automatic source\ndetection never leaves the Vite root. Anything used exclusively in\nui/tucu-docs was therefore never emitted — every `via-*` stop among them,\nso the feature-card gradients on the home page lost their middle colour or\nrendered grey.\n\nPoint the app at the library''s `./theme` entry instead of the compiled\n`./styles` one, as tucu-ui''s own docs prescribe for a consumer that runs\nits own Tailwind, and declare both source roots explicitly. Reading from\nui/tucu-ui/src rather than dist/ also means local library changes show up\nwithout rebuilding the package first, which is the reason this app exists.\n\nMeasured on a clean build: 4425 KB of CSS down to 1697 KB (-61.7%) while\nthe emitted class count rises from 3207 to 3413. The four classes that\ndisappear (bg-gray-700/90, border-gray-200, dark:bg-dark,\ndark:border-gray-700) are unused anywhere in the workspace.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgW0Xzwxyw7EbDV9DSOn/ap7+0ee\nwK0skFba86dVZgcpQAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOsHcEVjZ/PqjWywl5KxjMsESwspitO0OZsZA1aqhBEVZclNhrBdcE41WtViiNCTfo\neJPTkQntWMYTYVsoVUWgI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-01T18:36:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71472902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos","id":71472902,"login":"e-burgos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDcyOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commit/33843c0791f55a594481cde47d2693a4a1d69f01","node_id":"C_kwDOMrriatoAKDMzODQzYzA3OTFmNTVhNTk0NDgxY2RlNDdkMjY5M2E0YTFkNjlmMDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commit/04710e7a42c871aacdfa71095ff43c7657527f63","sha":"04710e7a42c871aacdfa71095ff43c7657527f63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commits/04710e7a42c871aacdfa71095ff43c7657527f63"}],"sha":"33843c0791f55a594481cde47d2693a4a1d69f01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commits/33843c0791f55a594481cde47d2693a4a1d69f01"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71472902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos","id":71472902,"login":"e-burgos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDcyOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commits/04710e7a42c871aacdfa71095ff43c7657527f63/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-01T16:28:53Z","email":"estebanburgos85@gmail.com","name":"Esteban Burgos"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T16:28:53Z","email":"estebanburgos85@gmail.com","name":"Esteban Burgos"},"message":"docs(docs): document the BasicTable mobile card layout\n\nAdd a \"Mobile Card Layout\" section explaining the behaviour and why it is\nCSS-only. The live demo uses cardBreakpoint=\"lg\" so the card layout is\nreachable by narrowing a desktop window rather than needing a phone, and a\nsecond table shows the mobileCards={false} opt-out.\n\nExpose mobileCards and cardBreakpoint in the playground with their real\ndefaults, extend the code example, and mention the layout in the hero.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0e5836a4487f80eeda832958210e23840ce9f113","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/git/trees/0e5836a4487f80eeda832958210e23840ce9f113"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/git/commits/04710e7a42c871aacdfa71095ff43c7657527f63","verification":{"payload":"tree 0e5836a4487f80eeda832958210e23840ce9f113\nparent 58425bc113692bced77e2907c26693d8238ab97c\nauthor Esteban Burgos <estebanburgos85@gmail.com> 1785601733 -0300\ncommitter Esteban Burgos <estebanburgos85@gmail.com> 1785601733 -0300\n\ndocs(docs): document the BasicTable mobile card layout\n\nAdd a \"Mobile Card Layout\" section explaining the behaviour and why it is\nCSS-only. The live demo uses cardBreakpoint=\"lg\" so the card layout is\nreachable by narrowing a desktop window rather than needing a phone, and a\nsecond table shows the mobileCards={false} opt-out.\n\nExpose mobileCards and cardBreakpoint in the playground with their real\ndefaults, extend the code example, and mention the layout in the hero.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgW0Xzwxyw7EbDV9DSOn/ap7+0ee\nwK0skFba86dVZgcpQAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJYVprlCGlNv0bzA0GNl0WQoiLxpL1JO9uR6V5cZF4hn5mPDWly599XHdvDOerJSXf\n3orAsfB2X9CBl4gczPHQM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-01T18:36:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71472902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/following{/other_