er, and drops one redundant lookup\nper call.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3c6250d7078c3ffb464b69436bac3ff06e606bb3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/git/trees/3c6250d7078c3ffb464b69436bac3ff06e606bb3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/git/commits/af36db700c82a89915282ef78d94078730548c13","verification":{"payload":"tree 3c6250d7078c3ffb464b69436bac3ff06e606bb3\nparent 01dae1f48013f2cda460c38d26ad8c6cbaa6c724\nauthor Esteban Burgos <estebanburgos85@gmail.com> 1785592513 -0300\ncommitter Esteban Burgos <estebanburgos85@gmail.com> 1785592513 -0300\n\nrefactor(ui): drop non-null assertions in favour of real narrowing\n\nBoth sites did a `Map.has` / `Map.set` dance and then re-read the map with\na `!` assertion. Reading once and branching on the result is shorter, gets\nthe same guarantee from the type checker, and drops one redundant lookup\nper call.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgW0Xzwxyw7EbDV9DSOn/ap7+0ee\nwK0skFba86dVZgcpQAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQH0S/7ehD61DMJJN8aetTeGfvwpwNATtkl4UoR66xQbBxO98YA8gsXXmoMUdtE+QAb\nezBmjOD8CJhM7Yz1tYEwc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-01T18:36:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71472902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos","id":71472902,"login":"e-burgos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDcyOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commit/af36db700c82a89915282ef78d94078730548c13","node_id":"C_kwDOMrriatoAKGFmMzZkYjcwMGM4MmE4OTkxNTI4MmVmNzhkOTQwNzg3MzA1NDhjMTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commit/01dae1f48013f2cda460c38d26ad8c6cbaa6c724","sha":"01dae1f48013f2cda460c38d26ad8c6cbaa6c724","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commits/01dae1f48013f2cda460c38d26ad8c6cbaa6c724"}],"sha":"af36db700c82a89915282ef78d94078730548c13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commits/af36db700c82a89915282ef78d94078730548c13"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71472902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos","id":71472902,"login":"e-burgos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDcyOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commits/01dae1f48013f2cda460c38d26ad8c6cbaa6c724/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-01T13:54:56Z","email":"estebanburgos85@gmail.com","name":"Esteban Burgos"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T13:54:56Z","email":"estebanburgos85@gmail.com","name":"Esteban Burgos"},"message":"test(ui): make the tucu-ui test suite lint-clean\n\nThe suite carried 28 of the project''s 28 eslint errors and most of its\nwarnings. Fixed at the source rather than by relaxing rules:\n\n- carousel tests: hoist the component import to the top. Vitest hoists\n  vi.mock above every import, so the trailing import was never required\n  (import/first, 3).\n- macOS and input tests: replace no-op `() => {}` handler props with\n  `vi.fn()`, and `mockImplementation(() => {})` with `() => undefined`\n  (no-empty-function, 22).\n- setup.ts: make the framer-motion, swiper and recharts vi.mock factories\n  async and pull React in with `await import(''react'')` instead of\n  `require()` (no-var-requires, 3). Typing React properly also surfaced a\n  latent `unknown`/ReactNode mismatch in the motion proxy, now cast\n  explicitly.\n- setup.ts: drop the framer-motion-only props with an explicit omit list\n  instead of destructuring eight variables that were never read.\n- emoji test fixtures: give the wrapping spans role=\"img\" and an\n  aria-label (accessible-emoji, 9).\n- collapsible-menu: guard `closest(''div'')` instead of asserting non-null.\n- checkbox / list-item: remove the unused `vi` import.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"97dd97268d97bb769afdb011f44651af4d8b1c12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/git/trees/97dd97268d97bb769afdb011f44651af4d8b1c12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/git/commits/01dae1f48013f2cda460c38d26ad8c6cbaa6c724","verification":{"payload":"tree 97dd97268d97bb769afdb011f44651af4d8b1c12\nparent dcbb9f64df23561d30c1180bf296824c94251337\nauthor Esteban Burgos <estebanburgos85@gmail.com> 1785592496 -0300\ncommitter Esteban Burgos <estebanburgos85@gmail.com> 1785592496 -0300\n\ntest(ui): make the tucu-ui test suite lint-clean\n\nThe suite carried 28 of the project''s 28 eslint errors and most of its\nwarnings. Fixed at the source rather than by relaxing rules:\n\n- carousel tests: hoist the component import to the top. Vitest hoists\n  vi.mock above every import, so the trailing import was never required\n  (import/first, 3).\n- macOS and input tests: replace no-op `() => {}` handler props with\n  `vi.fn()`, and `mockImplementation(() => {})` with `() => undefined`\n  (no-empty-function, 22).\n- setup.ts: make the framer-motion, swiper and recharts vi.mock factories\n  async and pull React in with `await import(''react'')` instead of\n  `require()` (no-var-requires, 3). Typing React properly also surfaced a\n  latent `unknown`/ReactNode mismatch in the motion proxy, now cast\n  explicitly.\n- setup.ts: drop the framer-motion-only props with an explicit omit list\n  instead of destructuring eight variables that were never read.\n- emoji test fixtures: give the wrapping spans role=\"img\" and an\n  aria-label (accessible-emoji, 9).\n- collapsible-menu: guard `closest(''div'')` instead of asserting non-null.\n- checkbox / list-item: remove the unused `vi` import.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgW0Xzwxyw7EbDV9DSOn/ap7+0ee\nwK0skFba86dVZgcpQAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQABgbbOqXIVyqFzLxGIvj3A0TQylQybU8GIlenhxuqQN4JWnWL9GnRGMg5huid8dkT\ncuXBod2i7ulevpBZ7K5gU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-01T18:36:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71472902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/use