aLa\nUmXdXsKPpcMefCHChiJQA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-15T22:06:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71472902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos","id":71472902,"login":"e-burgos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDcyOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commit/34e054253e406ff2c6fbf3bd61904e554800e17c","node_id":"C_kwDOMrriatoAKDM0ZTA1NDI1M2U0MDZmZjJjNmZiZjNiZDYxOTA0ZTU1NDgwMGUxN2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commit/bcc3741db03c12002def5534d60238dc38e0b624","sha":"bcc3741db03c12002def5534d60238dc38e0b624","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commits/bcc3741db03c12002def5534d60238dc38e0b624"}],"sha":"34e054253e406ff2c6fbf3bd61904e554800e17c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commits/34e054253e406ff2c6fbf3bd61904e554800e17c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71472902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos","id":71472902,"login":"e-burgos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDcyOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commits/bcc3741db03c12002def5534d60238dc38e0b624/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T22:06:01Z","email":"estebanburgos85@gmail.com","name":"Esteban Burgos"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T22:06:01Z","email":"estebanburgos85@gmail.com","name":"Esteban Burgos"},"message":"feat(ui): add a tokens-only ./theme export for Tailwind consumers (WS2)\n\nImplements WS2 (CSS-1, CSS-3, CSS-4) from the audit spec: a consumer\nalready running Tailwind v4 no longer needs a second full Tailwind\ninstance just to get tucu-ui''s tokens and component styles.\n\n- New `./theme` export (theme.css): @theme tokens + base.css/\n  third-party.css re-scoped into Tailwind''s own `base`/`components`\n  layers + tucu- prefixed @utility registrations. No `@import\n  ''tailwindcss''`, no preflight, no generated utilities — copied\n  verbatim to dist (not run through this library''s own Tailwind\n  build) so the directives reach the consumer''s compiler unprocessed.\n\n- base.css''s html:root/html.dark rules move from unlayered (always\n  wins, defeats consumer CSS by design) into `@layer base`; third-\n  party.css''s swiper/recharts overrides move into `@layer components`.\n  Verified empirically (a scratch Tailwind v4 + Vite consumer, both\n  import orders): Tailwind v4 fixes the theme/base/components/\n  utilities layer order via `@import ''tailwindcss''` regardless of\n  where a `@layer base {...}`/`@layer components {...}` block using\n  those same names appears relative to that import — using Tailwind''s\n  own layer names here (instead of a new custom one, as the spec\n  suggested) is what makes consumer utilities reliably win regardless\n  of import order, satisfying CSS-1''s acceptance criterion.\n\n- Custom utilities (text-h1, text-body, animation-delay-200, etc.)\n  renamed with a tucu- prefix to avoid colliding with a consumer''s own\n  utility names; unprefixed names kept as deprecated @apply aliases in\n  legacy-utilities.css, imported only by the `./styles` (globals.css)\n  path. The 3 internal component files using the old names (typography,\n  loader, select) were updated to the prefixed versions.\n\n- globals.css (the `./styles` export) now imports theme.css + Tailwind\n  + legacy-utilities.css, so both exports share one canonical source\n  for tokens/base/components/utilities instead of duplicating them.\n\nScope note: macOS theme CSS (~14K lines, opt-in via html.macos/\nhtml.macos-tahoe classes) ships as-is via theme.css''s import chain,\nunlayered — it doesn''t have the \"always wins on every page\" problem\nbase.css had, since it only applies once a consumer opts into that\ntheme variant.\n\nVerified: full test suite (482 tests), typecheck, and lint all pass\nwith no new issues. Visual pass over the real demo app (framer-motion,\nswiper, recharts, macOS Sonoma/Tahoe themes, typography scale,\nloaders) shows no regressions.","tree":{"sha":"e6d8d457914a65f108b3601ff9d596474405dad4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/git/trees/e6d8d457914a65f108b3601ff9d596474405dad4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/git/commits/bcc3741db03c12002def5534d60238dc38e0b624","verification":{"payload":"tree e6d8d457914a65f108b3601ff9d596474405dad4\nparent d3c849ea2385bc4a99615ddd51daf70dd9524346\nauthor Esteban Burgos <estebanburgos85@gmail.com> 1784153161 -0300\ncommitter Esteban Burgos <estebanburgos85@gmail.com> 1784153161 -0300\n\nfeat(ui): add a tokens-only ./theme export for Tailwind consumers (WS2)\n\nImplements WS2 (CSS-1, CSS-3, CSS-4) from the audit spec: a consumer\nalready running Tailwind v4 no longer needs a second full Tailwind\ninstance just to get tucu-ui''s tokens and component styles.\n\n- New `./theme` export (theme.css): @theme tokens + base.css/\n  third-party.css re-scoped into Tailwind''s own `base`/`components`\n  layers + tucu- prefixed @utility registrations. No `@import\n  ''tailwindcss''`, no preflight, no generated utilities — copied\n  verbatim to dist (not run through this library''s own Tailwind\n  build) so the directives reach the consumer''s compiler unprocessed.\n\n- base.css''s html:root/html.dark rules move from unlayered (always\n  wins, defeats consumer CSS by design) into `@layer base`; third-\n  party.css''s swiper/recharts overrides move into `@layer components`.\n  Verified empirically (a scratch Tailwind v4 + Vite consumer, both\n  import orders): Tailwind v4 fixes the theme/base/components/\n  utilities layer order via `@import ''tailwindcss''` regardless of\n  where a `@layer base {...}`/`@layer components {...}` block using\n  those same names appears relative to that import — using Tailwind''s\n  own layer names here (instead of a new custom one, as the spec\n  suggested) is what makes consumer utilities reliably win regardless\n  of import order, satisfying CSS-1''s acceptance criterion.\n\n- Custom utilities (text-h1, text-body, animation-delay-200, etc.)\n  renamed with a tucu- prefix to avoid colliding with a consumer''s own\n  utility names; unprefixed names kept as deprecated @apply aliases in\n  legacy-utilities.css, imported only by the `./styles` (globals.css)\n  path. The 3 internal component files using the old names (typography,\n  loader, select) were updated to the prefixed versions.\n\n- globals.css (the `./styles` export) now imports theme.css + Tailwind\n  + legacy-utilities.css, so both exports share one canonical source\n  for tokens/base/components/utilities instead of duplicating them.\n\nScope note: macOS theme CSS (~14K lines, opt-in via html.macos/\nhtml.macos-tahoe classes) ships as-is via theme.css''s import chain,\nunlayered — it doesn''t have the \"always wins on every page\" problem\nbase.css had, since it only applies once a consumer opts into that\ntheme variant.\n\nVerified: full test suite (482 tests), typecheck, and lint all pass\nwith no new issues. Visual pass over the real demo app (framer-motion,\nswiper, recharts, macOS Sonoma/Tahoe themes, typography scale,\nloaders) shows no regressions.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgW0Xzwxyw7EbDV9DSOn/ap7+0ee\nwK0skFba86dVZgcpQAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJHYwkQz1ipkN3va6EGDQpquVXFnsxF14nYITZzv/jk6/siKCRf7buYxpAXcrrbjqQ\niyhqQbFW7wWTUFGAI1fQA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-15T22:06:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71472902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos","id":71472902,"login":"e-burgos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDcyOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commit/bcc3741db03c12002def5534d60238dc38e0b624","node_id":"C_kwDOMrriatoAKGJjYzM3NDFkYjAzYzEyMDAyZGVmNTUzNGQ2MDIzOGRjMzhlMGI2MjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commit/d3c849ea2385bc4a99615ddd51daf70dd9524346","sha":"d3c849ea2385bc4a99615ddd51daf70dd9524346","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commits/d3c849ea2385bc4a99615ddd51daf70dd9524346"}],"sha":"bcc3741db03c12002def5534d60238dc38e0b624","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commits/bcc3741db03c12002def5534d60238dc38e0b624"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71472902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/e-burgos","id":71472902,"login":"e-burgos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDcyOTAy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/e-burgos","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/commits/d3c849ea2385bc4a99615ddd51daf70dd9524346/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T21:39:24Z","email":"estebanburgos85@gmail.com","name":"Esteban Burgos"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T21:39:24Z","email":"estebanburgos85@gmail.com","name":"Esteban Burgos"},"message":"fix(ui): stop scanning third-party node_modules for Tailwind classes\n\nframer-motion and recharts style through inline style props, lucide-react\nrenders raw SVG, and swiper ships its own hand-written CSS (imported\nseparately) — none of them author Tailwind class names in their own\nsource, so scanning their node_modules only produced junk utilities.\n\nVerified visually against the real published package: framer-motion\nanimations, lucide icons, the swiper carousel, and recharts charts all\nstill render correctly (a pre-existing, unrelated bug in the BarChart\ndemo — missing bar rects — reproduces identically with and without this\nchange, confirming it isn''t a regression from this fix).","tree":{"sha":"9e5d994d1fdf0210d85605bae2f7fe7375f8e45a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/git/trees/9e5d994d1fdf0210d85605bae2f7fe7375f8e45a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e-burgos/tucu-ui/git/commits/d3c849ea2385bc4a99615ddd51daf70dd9524346","verification":{"payload":"tree 9e5d994d1fdf0210d85605bae2f7fe7375f8e45a\nparent 653df6f5744b25d45018b4e6e050063fa9f8e31d\nauthor Esteban Burgos <estebanburgos85@gmail.com> 1784151564 -0300\ncommitter Esteban Burgos <estebanburgos85@gmail.com> 1784151564 -0300\n\nfix(ui): stop scanning third-party node_modules for Tailwind classes\n\nframer-motion and recharts style through inline style props, lucide-react\nrenders raw SVG, and swiper ships its own hand-written CSS (imported\nseparately) — none of them author Tailwind class names in their own\nsource, so scanning their node_modules only produced junk utilities.\n\nVerified visually against the real published package: framer-motion\nanimations, lucide icons, the swiper carousel, and recharts charts all\nstill render correctly (a pre-existing, unrelated bug in the BarChart\ndemo — missing bar rects — reproduces identically with and without this\nchange, confirming it isn''t a regression from this fix).\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgW0Xzwxyw7EbDV9DSOn/ap7+0ee\nwK0sk